WEBVTT

NOTE
Synthetic platform-neutral daily standup transcript
Sprint 01 | Day 04 of 10 | 2026-04-09 | Focus: Saved-cart merge

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:57.000
<v Jane Doe>Morning, folks. Day 04 of the sprint. We did the walkthrough, and the line-level response is clearer. The inventory spec is available now, but the gateway scope wasn’t included. Emily?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:59.000
<v Emily Davis>I can read the spec but can’t call the endpoint. I get 403. The access ticket said inventory access, not which gateway or environment.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:03:01.000
<v Robert Taylor>The role is for dev, not test. I’ll request the test scope. I’ve started listing principal, environment, and action in the access notes.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:04:03.000
<v Michael Brown>I’ve got the merge ID and result endpoint. The frontend can fetch status. There’s a 409 if the same ID is submitted again.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:57.000
<v David Wilson>I’m getting a 409 when I retry after a timeout, but I don’t know whether the first request completed. Could the endpoint return the existing result for that ID?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:06:07.000
<v Michael Brown>That’s better. I treated it as a conflict, not an idempotent retry. I’ll change it to return the original result.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:07:09.000
<v Alex Smith>Good. Keep a separate conflict for a different payload using the same ID.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:08:11.000
<v Sarah Miller>I found a mismatch in the capped quantity. The response says merged quantity three, but the cart shows four after refresh.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:09:13.000
<v Michael Brown>I think the saved cart is being reloaded before the merge transaction commits. I’ll check. We didn’t see it in the earlier cart test because it only covered the single-session flow.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:10:15.000
<v David Wilson>That could be why the count flickers too. I can wait on the result endpoint before refreshing the page.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:11:09.000
<v Sarah Miller>Please don’t patch around it until Michael checks the server flow. I can hold the integrated test for an hour.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:12:19.000
<v Jane Doe>What does that do to your slot?

00:12:32.000 --> 00:13:21.000
<v Sarah Miller>If it’s ready by eleven, I can keep the slot. After that I lose it to the payment team.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:14:23.000
<v Robert Taylor>The scope request is approved, but the secret isn’t mounted in test. The service account needs a separate grant.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:15:25.000
<v Michael Brown>That’s new to me. I can run the query locally, but not the integrated path.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:16:27.000
<v Alex Smith>I have three PRs waiting and a release review at noon. I’ll take the API behavior; Emily can review the query once access works.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:17:21.000
<v Emily Davis>I can review it after lunch, but I can’t test the gateway today if the secret is still missing.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:18:31.000
<v John Doe>Product changed the delisted-item rule: preserve the item but make checkout unavailable. That’s the same display as out of stock, right?

00:18:44.000 --> 00:19:33.000
<v David Wilson>Mostly. I can show “unavailable,” but should the shopper still be able to remove it?

00:19:46.000 --> 00:20:35.000
<v John Doe>Yes. I’ll add that and stop changing the rule after this.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:21:29.000
<v Jane Doe>The walkthrough caught the duplicate line case, but we still didn’t check the test gateway permission. Robert, update the checklist and exact owner. Sarah, run the duplicate-cart cases while we wait.
